00:00:02.629 --> 00:00:04.730 align:start position:0%
it goes without saying that ace and his  role in the story of one piece have been  a wildly controversial topic many adore  his character for it's cool and charming  design while many others criticize it  for its lack of character development  and impulsive behavior and at the height  of this debate stands of course the  climax of Asus tragic story arc his  defeat by Blackbeard is captured by the  Marines his liberation by Luffy and  finally his sacrifice for his younger  brother a common point of criticism  regarding Asus death is that ace did not  have enough character development to  make his death feel impactful enough and  while emotional connection to a  character is and always will be a  subjective experience for every one of  us I find that this argument is somewhat  missing the point of Asus role in the  story because not every character in a  story can or even should undergo  character development in fact there are  three types of character are ecstatic  character can go through positive change  negative change or no change at all  ace just as many other important side  characters in the story has a flat  character arc meaning he doesn't change  his view on the world but stays a  constant throughout his appearances in  the story his entire life  ace is struggling with the legacy of his  father's name having to suffer under  both the burning hatred as well as the  flaming admiration people had for Roger  being born as the son of the worst  criminal of his age until his very last  moment ace is struggling to find meaning  in his life and whether he ever deserved  to live in the first place the one thing  he can cling on to is his burning will  to protect his friends and family from  any harm his death therefore was one of  the most shocking events in the entirety  of one piece especially so since Oda is  very careful and averse when it comes to  killing of characters and most  importantly ASUS death was not a Disney  death where the person suddenly comes  back to life in the end know what makes  this moment so incredibly powerful is  that it is final and  real consequences and therefore in this  video I want to talk about the tragedy  of portgas the ace and why his death is  one of the fundamental cornerstones of  the wampie story because Luffy losing  his beloved older brother not only  deepens our protagonist character but it  also advances the plot in a crucial way  and of course also impacts us the  readers emotionally when I talk about  how aces death has deepened Luffy's  character I believe it goes much deeper  than simply showing Luffy that he has to  become stronger in fact Luffy already  was aware of this back on water 7 when  he talks to Bruno about his devastating  defeat by LKG and of course losing his  crew to Kees ruined Cunha against both  of whom he stood not the slightest  chance also made Luffy realized that he  had to become much more powerful so no  aces death was not simply a way for  Luffy to become stronger losing his  treasured older brother whom he had  shared such a happy and adventurous  childhood with shook luffy to his core  and from there developed his character  fundamentally having his loving bond  with his brother cut just when he had  managed to finally do the impossible and  save him from the marines through luffy  into deep distress and despair being  characterized by his positive easygoing  and at times in the evening  Luffy has to learn that not every  obstacle can be overcome through  determination alone for the first time  ever he was not able to fulfill a goal  he set himself he gave everything he had  to save his brother and he still failed  he realizes that loss and failure are  things that can actually happen to him  if he's not willing to take things  seriously but it goes even further than  this it makes Luffy question his entire  purpose for setting out to see losing  both his crew and ace is an absolute low  point in his adventure however the  experience allows him to realize that  his crew are not only his friends but  family and that he has to grow  significantly in order to be able to  protect them from aces fate  thus he literally inherits aces will to  protect those he holds dear at any cost  it is the decisive trigger for Luffy to  become the powerful and more mature  captain that he is today and finally  seeing his brother murdered in front of  his own eyes also gave Luffy his first  ever antagonist that he resents on a  personal level  killing ace and literally burning the  mark of his death into Lucy's chest is a  permanent visual reminder of what the  Admiral did to our protagonist in the  end Luffy comes out of his grief as a  stronger wiser and overall more mature  captain facing a strong antagonist that  he truly resents with all his heart  but ASIS tragic character arc does even  more for the story than just developing  Luffy it advances the plotline  significantly and sets the stage for the  second half of the story  well some people disliked aces defeat by  Blackbeard and his subsequent capture by  the Marines these events not only  introduced Blackbeard as Luffy's biggest  rival for the story but it also placed  Luffy as aces little brother right at  the center of the imple down at marine  for arts this was crucial  since both arcs did not only introduce a  ton of new important characters but also  rang in the end of rogers and white bits  era and the beginning of the new age  since s wanted to make white beard king  of the Pirates and white beard in turn  to make a spirit King there was very  little room for Luffy to come closer to  his goal  this new power vacuum created by white  beards death was not only convenient but  necessary for both Luffy and Blackbeard  to have a realistic shot at finding the  one piece and this war taking place and  Luffy being able to be present there was  only possible because his adopted  brother  the son of the former pirate king  himself was to be publicly executed and  politicized by the world government and  beside that the war and luffy's tragic  loss also served as a midpoint climax to  the entire series which gave the  adventure a fresh start of the time skip  and better pacing overall in this  context it also allowed us to see Luffy  reflect upon his childhood with ace and  Sabo and thus gave us a much deeper look  into the development and history of his  character so to put it shortly  aces character was designed to enable  crucial plot development for the one  piece story that resulted in one of the  most popular arcs of the series and also  set the stage for the second half of the  adventure in the new world  now it would be quite heartless of me of  course  to say that Asus character was simply an  elegant tool smartly fit into the story  to develop Luffy and the plots because  as I said at the beginning for many days  was a deeply likeable character thus his  death obviously had a strong emotional  impact on his readers as well however  even if you did not like or care for ace  too much before his execution I think  that the moment he died was nonetheless  powerful for pretty much any reader  because not only that a sacrifices just  be gained life for his little brother  Luffy but Oda also found a quite  emotional and yet weirdly satisfying end  to his character arc firstly the true  magnitude of a minor characters death is  always defined by the reaction of the  hero who we all emphasize with and  luffy's reaction to aces death might  very well be the most powerful and  heartbreaking thing we've had to witness  in the entire series so far this fact  alone gave this moment and thus aces  character a lot of meaning actually  making him even more popular after his  death and secondly ace finally managed  to find an answer to the question that  has haunted him his entire life why do I  live all his life ace was known for  never turning his back on an enemy no  matter how strong they were and when he  finally accepts white beard and his men  as his new family he proudly wears his  mark on his back where it could never be  harmed and yet despite this pride the  last thing he does is turning his back  on a canoe in order to protect his  family having Luffy and white beard  taking on the world government itself  for his sake shows him that people  actually do care whether he lives or not  he actually deserves to live and so just  having found his answer he chooses to  protect his family over all else and  this will he then inherits - Luffy  what we can take away from all this is  that Asus character is much more than a  cool older brother whose death motivated  Luffy to train for two years and get  stronger know the hardship and doubt  that he carried in his heart for his  entire life as well as the love that he  felt for his family led to the most  impactful event in the story up to this  point not only did he give significant  character development to Luffy but he  also shaped and developed a plot of the  story in a number of crucial ways and in  the end his death drove home one of the  most if not the most important theme in  one piece  following your dreams because with ace  dying in the end with a smile on his  face just as his father did Oda tells us  that if you pursue your dream and strive  for what you really wanted in life you  will have a happy ending  [Music]  hey everyone thank you so much for  watching what are your thoughts on ace  and the story and what character would  you like to see me discuss next share  your thoughts with me in the comments  below if you enjoy one piece and want to  learn more about storytelling world  building or my thoughts on the latest  one piece chapter make sure to LIKE and  subscribe to become part of the channel  right now I hope to see around next time  and until then stay safe and have a  wonderful week  you  you
 

